# TYPE-RETIREMENT MARKER DEDUP reseed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT ENTERS (committed to `src/` on fix/retirement in this same change):
#   - checker (`type.tks`): `type_eq` now equates the backend markers `Error{}` / `Null{}` with a nominal
#     reference to the checker's own `type Error` / `type Null` (`Named{"teko::checker::Error"}` /
#     `Named{"teko::checker::Null"}`) — the form `@Type()`'s `Error` / `Null` members resolve to. They are
#     the SAME element; the nominal `type Type = variant … | Error | … | Null` only KEPT them apart because
#     it was opaque. `from_is_bare_null` is deliberately NOT widened, so a nominal `…::Null` member is never
#     hoisted as a nullable-union absence marker (which would reshape the `Type` variant and break its
#     exhaustiveness), and `resolve_named` is untouched, so `Error { }` / `Null { }` STRUCT construction
#     still resolves the nominal struct.
#   - checker (`resolve.tks`): `union_dedup` drops `type_eq` duplicate members WITHOUT flattening (unlike
#     `union_collect`, which `type_join` uses), and `resolve_type`'s `UnionType` arm runs it before
#     `union_normalize_null`. An annotated `@Type() | error` / `@Type() | null` — the surface adds the case
#     the `@Type()` already carries — collapses to ONE member instead of two members mangling to the one
#     backend tag (`TK_TAG_…_ERROR` / `_NULL`, a C enumerator redeclaration).
#   Carried forward from the prior reseeds: §9.D CR1/CR2/CR3, the union-of-unions nested group-option,
#   §14 A0-A4 / B1-B5, §14 Form 2 parametric type-macros, §9.D capabilities (a)/(b)/(c), and the §9.D sweep
#   so far (31 unions retired before this reseed, TStatement last).
